From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sw: default fly/draw object names in O(1) amortised (WASM only) (FG-141)

PDF import into Writer creates one frame per glyph line plus one shape per
path (vision2030: ~43,000 objects). lcl_GetUniqueFlyName walked every object
for every new name: O(N^2), measured 282 s of a 310 s emit phase. Under
__EMSCRIPTEN__ each SwDoc keeps a per-prefix monotonic counter plus a superset
of numbers above it that may be in use; SdrObject names (not indexed) are
learned by one full walk and then from a small svx ring buffer fed by
SdrObject::SetName and SdrObjList insertion. Ring wrap -> full walk again;
counter overflow -> the upstream walk. Upstream's own fix (a61128c95e32) was
reverted (f1c247acd6b8) only because UITests rely on predictable names.

Behaviour difference (all Writer documents, WASM build): names stay unique,
but a number freed by deleting or renaming an object is never reused, so an
import that creates then deletes a frame yields e.g. "Frame3" where upstream
gives "Frame2". Such names are written to DOCX (wp:docPr name) and ODT
(draw:name); nothing compares them. Measured after: 43,000 names in 142 ms;
vision2030 PDF -> DOCX 60 s (was failing), 11,294 text boxes, no duplicates.
---
